    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "exactly. it feels like the debate gets stuck in these loops about tax percentages while the world is literally changing under our feet. if the goal is to actually prevent that collapse, shouldn't we just stop pretending that traditional fiscal policy is even applicable to an era of AI-driven abundance? like, is the old way of thinking just fundamentally broken for this new reality?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
